entries.contract:
Connect to Robinhood's official Trading MCP server.

List the user's brokerage accounts. Each account includes an agentic_allowed field indicating whether it's tradable by you — accounts where it's false are read-only to you. Use this to look up account_number values needed by other tools. Exactly one account is tradable by you; when the user is choosing an account for a trade, use that account directly without asking. Does NOT return reliable buying power — route buying-power questions through get_portfolio.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__robinhood_trading_get_accounts(args: {}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.
  data: {
  // The user's brokerage accounts. Empty when the user has none.
  accounts: null | Array<null | {
  // Brokerage account number; pass to any tool that requires account_number. Mask all but the last 4 digits (e.g. '••••1234') when displaying to the user.
  account_number: string;
  // Affiliate / region code (e.g. 'RHF', 'RHUK', 'RHSG'). Affects feature availability for the account.
  affiliate?: string;
  // True when this account is accessible to this agent specifically. An account with false may be agentic-enabled but scoped to a different agent type — do not tell the user it is disabled. Sole source of truth for eligibility — never infer it from nickname text. review_*/place_*/cancel_* tools reject accounts where this is false.
  agentic_allowed: boolean;
  // Account type, e.g. 'individual', 'ira_traditional', 'ira_roth', 'ira_traditional_inherited', 'ira_roth_inherited', 'isa_stocks_and_shares'.
  brokerage_account_type: string;
  // True when the account is currently deactivated.
  deactivated: boolean;
  // True for the user's default account. Surface when choosing among multiple accounts.
  is_default: boolean;
  // Management classification (e.g. 'managed') when applicable; layered on top of brokerage_account_type rather than replacing it.
  management_type?: string;
  // User-set nickname; present alongside account_number when set. Cosmetic only — not an agentic_allowed or agentic-account signal.
  nickname?: string;
  // Options approval: 'option_level_2' (long calls/puts, covered calls, cash-secured puts), 'option_level_3' (spreads and complex strategies), or empty/'option_level_0' (not approved).
  option_level: string;
  // True when the account is permanently closed (cannot be reactivated).
  permanently_deactivated: boolean;
  // Crypto account number for this account (e.g. 'RHC1234567'). Absent when no linked crypto account exists. Mask all but the last 4 digits (e.g. '••••1234') when displaying to the user.
  rhc_account_number?: string;
  // Numeric brokerage account number — pass this (not account_number) to any nummus-backed tool that asks for an account identifier.
  rhs_account_number: string;
  // Account state — 'active' is normal; anything else (deactivated, restricted, etc.) means the account cannot trade normally.
  state: string;
  // 'cash', 'margin', or 'limited_margin' — the trading-permissions classification for the brokerage account. 'limited_margin' (instant settlement without full margin leverage) applies to accounts where full margin is unavailable, such as retirement (IRA), managed, and agentic accounts. Crypto accounts are never marginable, so a linked crypto account has no equivalent.
  type: string;
  // Proceeds from recent sales not yet settled (cash accounts settle T+1), in the account's currency. Informational only and may lag live trading — this is NOT a spendable or order-gating figure; buying_power from get_portfolio is authoritative for what can be traded now. A cash-type account with unsettled_funds greater than 0 could trade with those proceeds immediately by upgrading to limited margin. Absent when upstream does not report it — treat as unknown, not zero.
  unsettled_funds?: string;
  // The caller's own options approval on a multi-member (trust) account: 'option_level_2', 'option_level_3', or absent. Absent on single-owner and joint accounts and whenever the caller holds no level of their own. When present and below option_level the caller is view-only for options on this account and cannot place, replace, cancel or exercise; treat user_option_level, not option_level, as their tradable level.
  user_option_level?: string;
}>;
};
  // Sort the list deterministically when presenting: the default account first, agentic accounts (agentic_allowed=true) second, then other individual accounts, then retirement (IRA) accounts. Present account_number, rhc_account_number (label it "Crypto Account"), brokerage_account_type (label it "Account Type" — a linked crypto account always shares it, so never add a separate crypto account type column), type (label it "Brokerage Trading Type"), nickname (if set), and is_default — in that column order. In the Crypto Account column show "N/A" for accounts with an empty rhc_account_number; omit the column entirely only when no account has one. When referring to the account in user-facing prose (e.g. "your <X> account"), use nickname when set; fall back to brokerage_account_type otherwise. When displaying account_number or rhc_account_number to the user, mask all but the last 4 digits (e.g. '••••1234'); pass the full value to other tools unchanged — including get_option_level_upgrade_info and any fallback upgrade URL; masking breaks the link. Flag agentic_allowed when the user is choosing an account for a trade. There is exactly one agentic_allowed=true account — use it directly rather than asking which account to trade. agentic_allowed is caller-relative — true means accessible to this agent, false means this agent cannot act on it (the account may still be agentic-enabled for a different agent). Never state agentic_allowed's field name or raw boolean value to the user. Do not use nickname to determine agentic-account eligibility. Skip false accounts for trade operations; if the user asks why, say the account is not accessible to this agent, not that it needs to be enabled. When user_option_level is present (multi-member trust accounts), it is this user's own options level on that account and is the level to reason about for options actions there; if it is below option_level the user is view-only for options on that account. When user_option_level is absent on a trust account (brokerage_account_type='trust_revocable'), the user holds no options level of their own there — do not offer options actions on that account, even though option_level is set. When option_level is empty or 'option_level_0' and the user wants options, call get_option_level_upgrade_info with the account_number; if that tool is unavailable, direct the user to https://applink.robinhood.com/upgrade_options?account_number=<that account's account_number> (embed the full unmasked account_number in the URL). management_type='managed' is layered on brokerage_account_type — surface alongside, not as a replacement. For tools that ask for an account identifier on a crypto-backed flow (get_crypto_positions, future crypto write tools), pass rhs_account_number; for everything else (equities, options, etc.) pass account_number. Do not add an unsettled_funds column to the account table — surface it only via the following rule. Whenever you report an account's funds, value, or buying power and that account has type='cash' with unsettled_funds greater than 0, and the user wants to access unsettled funds or other features available in a limited margin account — if the get_limited_margin_upgrade_info tool is available — call it with the account_number and share the appropriate upgrade link. If that tool is not available, say nothing about limited margin (there is no fallback).
  guide: string;
}>>; };
```

Connect to Robinhood's official Trading MCP server.

Get the account's portfolio market value breakdown by asset type and buying power. Use for "how much is my account worth?", "what's my portfolio breakdown?", "how much do I have in options?", and "how much can I spend / afford?" questions.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__robinhood_trading_get_portfolio(args: {
  // Brokerage account number. Obtain from get_accounts.
  account_number: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.
  data: {
  // Real-time buying power from the broker.
  buying_power: null | {
  // Authoritative spendable figure used to gate order placement. For margin-enabled accounts it already includes available margin leverage; for cash and leverage-disabled accounts it equals the cash-only figure.
  buying_power: string;
  // Currency of the figures, e.g. 'USD'.
  display_currency: string;
  // Buying power for intraday leverage, when applicable; null when the account does not have intraday margin enabled.
  intraday_buying_power?: null | string;
  // Buying power outside the intraday-leverage window; null when not applicable.
  off_intraday_buying_power?: null | string;
  // Buying power ignoring margin leverage. Typically <= buying_power. Negative when the account is in deficit — new positions cannot be opened until the deficit is cleared.
  unleveraged_buying_power: string;
};
  // Available cash (includes early access from pending deposits).
  cash: string;
  // Spendable buying power for crypto buys. Cash-only (crypto is not marginable), so it excludes the equity margin leverage that buying_power may include — quote this for 'how much can I spend on crypto'. Omitted when unavailable.
  crypto_buying_power?: null | {
  // Authoritative spendable figure for crypto buys (cash-only; excludes equity margin leverage).
  buying_power: string;
};
  // Value of crypto holdings.
  crypto_value: string;
  // Currency all values are denominated in (e.g. USD).
  currency: string;
  // Value of stock and ETF positions.
  equity_value: string;
  // Value of event contract positions.
  event_contracts_value: string;
  // Value of fixed income instruments.
  fixed_income_value: string;
  // Value of futures positions (includes RHD cost basis).
  futures_value: string;
  // Value of mutual fund positions.
  mutual_funds_value: string;
  // Value of options positions.
  options_value: string;
  // Deposits in transit, not yet settled.
  pending_deposits: string;
  // Total portfolio value across all asset types. The default 'account value' to show the user.
  total_value: string;
};
  // Show total_value as "account value" or "portfolio value". The breakdown fields show how value is distributed across asset types. Zero-value fields mean the user has no holdings in that asset class — omit them from display unless the user explicitly asks. For "how much cash do I have?" use the cash field. buying_power is the real-time authoritative spendable figure from the broker; quote buying_power.buying_power as the primary affordability answer with buying_power.display_currency. For "how much can I spend on crypto?" quote crypto_buying_power.buying_power instead — crypto is cash-only (not marginable), so the top-level buying_power may overstate it; crypto_buying_power is omitted when unavailable. crypto_value reflects the user's crypto holdings value. On a cash account, recently sold proceeds that have not yet settled are not spendable and are not included in buying_power; that unsettled amount is reported as unsettled_funds by get_accounts (not here), so if you do not already have the account's unsettled_funds, call get_accounts to check it. Whenever you report buying power or account value for a type='cash' account whose unsettled_funds is greater than 0, and the user wants to access unsettled funds or other features available in a limited margin account — if the get_limited_margin_upgrade_info tool is available — call it with the account_number and share the appropriate upgrade link. If that tool is not available, say nothing about limited margin (there is no fallback).
  guide: string;
}>>; };
```

Connect to Robinhood's official Trading MCP server.

List open equity positions for a specific brokerage account. Returns symbol, quantity, average cost, and per-position hold breakdowns.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__robinhood_trading_get_equity_positions(args: {
  // Brokerage account number. Must come from the user or be clearly implied — never default from get_accounts.
  account_number: string;
  // Pagination cursor. Omit for the first page; for the next page, pass the prior response's next value back verbatim.
  cursor?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.
  data: {
  // Opaque cursor for the next page — NOT a URL. When non-empty more pages exist: call this tool again with cursor set to this value verbatim, leaving the other arguments unchanged. Empty on the last page.
  next?: string;
  // Open equity positions on this page. Empty when the cursor has no rows.
  positions: null | Array<null | {
  // Average cost per share as shown in the Robinhood app; reflects partial sells. Omitted for positions still reconciling.
  average_buy_price?: null | string;
  // Portion of quantity filled today (upstream is timezone-aware).
  intraday_quantity: string;
  // Total shares held, including today's fills. Negative for short positions.
  quantity: string;
  // Shares the user can sell right now (server-computed after subtracting holds).
  shares_available_for_sells: string;
  // Shares locked by an outgoing asset transfer (e.g. ACATS-out).
  shares_held_for_asset_transfer: string;
  // Shares earmarked for an upcoming options exercise/assignment.
  shares_held_for_options_events: string;
  // Shares locked by open outgoing sell orders.
  shares_held_for_sells: string;
  // Shares held for settlement of stock grants / unsettled inbound fills.
  shares_held_for_stock_grants: string;
  // Shares pending from an options exercise/assignment, not yet booked into quantity.
  shares_pending_from_options_events: string;
  // Ticker symbol.
  symbol: string;
  // 'long' (positive quantity), 'short' (negative), 'boxed' (both, rare), or 'empty' (zero).
  type: string;
}>;
};
  // Sellable shares: use shares_available_for_sells, not quantity. Yesterday's quantity = quantity - intraday_quantity. average_buy_price is the average cost per share shown in the Robinhood app (it already reflects partial sells) — use it as the user's average cost; it may be omitted for positions still reconciling. No market price here — for current value or PnL, call get_equity_quotes and multiply by quantity. Present symbol, quantity, average_buy_price, and type when not 'long'; suppress other fields unless asked.
  guide: string;
}>>; };
```

Connect to Robinhood's official Trading MCP server.

Fetch equity orders for an account — list mode (newest first; open and closed, including fills, cancellations, rejections) or single-order mode by passing order_id. When the user asks broadly for "orders" or "my orders" without naming an asset class or order type, call get_equity_orders, get_option_orders, get_crypto_orders, and get_advanced_orders in parallel so OCO groups are not omitted.

Filtering tips:
- Prefer narrow queries: combine state, symbol, and/or created_at_gte for specific questions (e.g. "my filled AAPL orders this week") — the per-page cap is fixed.
- created_at_gte: interpret relative times in the user's timezone, convert to UTC before sending.
- symbol forces a symbol→instrument lookup; omit it if you don't need it.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__robinhood_trading_get_equity_orders(args: {
  // Brokerage account number. Must come from the user or be clearly implied — never default from get_accounts.
  account_number: string;
  // Lower bound (inclusive). ISO 8601 UTC or YYYY-MM-DD; naive values are interpreted as UTC.
  created_at_gte?: string;
  // Pagination cursor. Omit for the first page; for the next page, pass the prior response's next value back verbatim.
  cursor?: string;
  // Filter to a single order by UUID. The response shape is unchanged (orders[] with at most one entry); empty when the order does not belong to account_number.
  order_id?: string;
  // Filter to one source: 'user', 'agentic' (MCP), 'recurring', 'drip', etc.
  placed_agent?: string;
  // Filter by single state: new, queued, confirmed, unconfirmed, partially_filled, filled, cancelled, rejected, failed, voided.
  state?: string;
  // Filter to one symbol (triggers a symbol→instrument lookup before the orders call).
  symbol?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.
  data: {
  // Opaque cursor for the next page — NOT a URL. When non-empty more pages exist: call this tool again with cursor set to this value verbatim, leaving the other arguments unchanged. Empty on the last page.
  next?: string;
  // Equity orders on this page, newest first. Empty when the cursor has no rows.
  orders: null | Array<null | {
  // Weighted average fill price across executions. Null until the first fill.
  average_price: null | string;
  // When the order was created.
  created_at: string;
  // Shares filled so far. Less than quantity while partially filled; equal once filled.
  cumulative_quantity: string;
  // Notional amount for dollar-based market orders; null for share-quantity orders.
  dollar_based_amount: null | {
  // Quoted-decimal amount, e.g. '100.00'.
  amount: string;
  // ISO currency code; always 'USD' for equity orders today.
  currency_code: string;
};
  // Per-fill detail; reference only for per-lot questions.
  executions: null | Array<{
  // Per-execution fees (regulatory + clearing) in USD.
  fees: string;
  // Execution UUID.
  id: string;
  // Fill price per share.
  price: string;
  // Shares filled in this execution.
  quantity: string;
  // When the fill occurred.
  timestamp: string;
}>;
  // Cumulative fees (regulatory + clearing) in USD.
  fees: string;
  // Order UUID; needed by cancel_equity_order.
  id: string;
  // Instrument UUID; resolve to symbol via the instruments endpoint if needed.
  instrument_id: string;
  // Time of the most recent fill, cancel, or reject. Null on a brand-new unfilled order.
  last_transaction_at: null | string;
  // 'regular_hours', 'extended_hours', or 'all_day_hours'.
  market_hours: string;
  // Source that placed the order: 'user' (app), 'agentic' (MCP), 'recurring', 'drip', 'brokeback' (system), or other internal values.
  placed_agent: string;
  // Limit price for limit/stop_limit orders; null for market orders.
  price: null | string;
  // Originally-requested share quantity. Null for dollar-based orders before the first fill.
  quantity: null | string;
  // Idempotency key the order is stored under, unique per account. Usually the ref_id passed to place_equity_order; an order placed through a trade approval carries that approval's id instead. Omitted when the order has none.
  ref_id?: string;
  // Free-text reason when state is 'rejected'.
  reject_reason?: string;
  // 'buy' or 'sell'.
  side: string;
  // Lifecycle state: new, queued, unconfirmed, partially_filled, filled, cancelled, rejected, failed, voided, pending_cancelled, partially_filled_rest_cancelled, and (for short-sale orders) locating, locate_failed.
  state: string;
  // Stop trigger price for stop_market/stop_limit orders; null otherwise.
  stop_price: null | string;
  // Ticker symbol.
  symbol: string;
  // 'gfd' (good for day) or 'gtc' (good till cancelled).
  time_in_force: string;
  // 'immediate' (market/limit) or 'stop' (stop_market/stop_limit).
  trigger: string;
  // Upstream type: 'market' or 'limit'. Combine with trigger to recover the user-facing market/limit/stop_market/stop_limit.
  type: string;
}>;
};
  // For dollar-based orders (dollar_based_amount populated, quantity sometimes null) describe in dollars until cumulative_quantity is meaningful. Mention placed_agent when it is not 'user'. Recover the user-facing order type from type+trigger or from price/stop_price. Present symbol, side, type, state, quantity (or dollar_based_amount), cumulative_quantity when partially filled, price for limit orders, average_price once filled, last_transaction_at (or created_at), and id when cancellation may follow; suppress other fields unless asked. When next is non-empty more pages exist — it is an opaque cursor, not a URL, so call this tool again with cursor set to that value verbatim and the same filters; keep paging until next is empty whenever the user asks for their full history.
  guide: string;
}>>; };
```

Connect to Robinhood's official Trading MCP server.

Get real-time stock quotes and the official last-completed-session close for one or more symbols.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__robinhood_trading_get_equity_quotes(args: {
  // One or more stock symbols. Above 20 symbols, quotes still return but closes is omitted with closes_error set.
  symbols: null | Array<string>;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.
  data: {
  // Populated when the closes lookup is skipped or fails tool-wide (e.g. too many symbols, upstream timeout, no previous_close_date). Per-symbol gaps surface as a missing close on the affected result, not here.
  closes_error?: string;
  // One entry per symbol resolved from /quotes/, in upstream order, each carrying the live quote and (when available) the official prior-session close. Empty if no symbol resolved.
  results: null | Array<null | {
  // Official settled close from the most recent completed session. Absent when closes_error is set, or when this symbol had no close in an otherwise-successful closes batch.
  close?: null | {
  // YYYY-MM-DD trading date for this close. May be earlier than the requested date when interpolated.
  date: null | string;
  // True when the requested date had no session and the price came from an earlier date.
  interpolated: null | boolean;
  // Official settled close price. Null when the upstream has no close (rare).
  price: null | string;
  // Upstream provenance (e.g. 'sip-close'). Informational.
  source: null | string;
  // Ticker symbol.
  symbol: string;
};
  // Live market data for this symbol.
  quote: null | {
  // Prior-day close adjusted for splits, dividends, and mergers.
  adjusted_previous_close: string;
  // Lowest current sell-order price. Zero when the book is closed or unavailable.
  ask_price: string;
  // Highest current buy-order price. Zero when the book is closed or unavailable.
  bid_price: string;
  // False for instruments that have never traded; price fields are meaningless when false.
  has_traded: boolean;
  // Most recent pre-market / after-hours / overnight trade. Null during regular hours or when the symbol does not trade in the current session.
  last_non_reg_trade_price: null | string;
  // Most recent regular-hours trade (9:30-16:00 ET). Stays frozen at the closing print after the close until the next open; not the official settled close.
  last_trade_price: string;
  // Raw prior closing print — not corporate-action adjusted and not the official settled close.
  previous_close: string;
  // YYYY-MM-DD trading date that previous_close corresponds to. Null for symbols that have never had a settled close.
  previous_close_date: null | string;
  // Instrument listing state — 'active' is normal; other values (inactive, delisted, unlisted) mean the instrument is not in normal trading state.
  state: string;
  // Ticker symbol.
  symbol: string;
  // Timestamp of ask_price.
  venue_ask_time: string;
  // Timestamp of bid_price.
  venue_bid_time: string;
  // Timestamp of last_non_reg_trade_price. Reveals which non-regular session the trade came from.
  venue_last_non_reg_trade_time: null | string;
  // Timestamp of last_trade_price.
  venue_last_trade_time: string;
};
}>;
};
  // Each entry in results pairs the live quote with the official prior-session close for the same symbol. Current price: pick whichever of quote.last_trade_price / quote.last_non_reg_trade_price has the more recent timestamp, then verify that timestamp is recent before calling it "current" — otherwise phrase as "as of <time>". Daily change uses quote.adjusted_previous_close. "Yesterday's close" uses results[].close.price (official settled close); when a result is missing close — either closes_error is set tool-wide, or this symbol had no close in an otherwise-successful batch — fall back to quote.previous_close and tell the user the official close lookup is unavailable. Drop bid/ask when zero. Surface has_traded=false or any non-'active' state before quoting a price.
  guide: string;
}>>; };
```

Connect to Robinhood's official Trading MCP server.

Check tradability for up to 10 equity symbols on a given account: per-session eligibility and fractional. Call before placing an order to surface restrictions. Exact-ticker match — no name or partial-ticker resolution.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__robinhood_trading_get_equity_tradability(args: {
  // Brokerage account number. Must come from the user or be clearly implied — never default from get_accounts.
  account_number: string;
  // Stock symbols, max 10 per call. With more than 10, split across multiple calls of 10 or fewer. Exact-ticker match only.
  symbols: null | Array<string>;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.
  data: {
  // Symbols that did not resolve (likely delisted, invalid, or non-equity).
  not_found?: null | Array<string>;
  // One entry per resolved symbol, in request order.
  results: null | Array<{
  // Per-account-type tradability for every account type the user's affiliate supports.
  account_type_tradabilities?: null | Array<{
  // Brokerage account type (e.g. 'individual', 'ira_traditional', 'ira_roth').
  account_type: string;
  // 'tradable', 'untradable', or 'position_closing_only' (sell-only).
  account_type_tradability: string;
}>;
  // Extended/all-day session (4 AM – 8 PM ET) eligibility. 'tradable' opens extended_hours and all_day_hours.
  all_day_tradability?: string;
  // ISO country code of the listing.
  country?: string;
  // Informational; effectively always false at order-placement today.
  extended_hours_fractional_tradability: boolean;
  // Decimal-quantity eligibility; non-'tradable' values require whole-share quantities.
  fractional_tradability?: string;
  // Human-readable halt details.
  internal_halt_details?: string;
  // ISO 8601 halt end.
  internal_halt_end_time?: string;
  // Internal halt reason (e.g. 'regulatory').
  internal_halt_reason?: string;
  // Sessions covered by the halt: any of 'regular_hours', 'extended_hours', 'all_day_hours'.
  internal_halt_sessions?: null | Array<string>;
  // ISO 8601 halt start.
  internal_halt_start_time?: string;
  // Full instrument name (e.g. 'Apple Inc. - Common Stock').
  name?: string;
  // Short-side eligibility; independent of long-side flags.
  short_selling_tradability?: string;
  // Short product name (e.g. 'Apple').
  simple_name?: string;
  // 'active' or 'inactive' (delisted/expired).
  state?: string;
  // Ticker symbol.
  symbol: string;
  // Listed and clearable on Robinhood; false routes nothing.
  tradeable: boolean;
  // Overnight 24/7 eligibility. Absent when the session is not applicable.
  twenty_four_seven_tradability?: string;
}>;
};
  // Use the account_type_tradabilities entry matching the user's account_type. If account_type_tradabilities is empty, report that account-type tradability could not be determined and rely on tradeable + state alone. Any of tradeable=false, state='inactive', or 'untradable' overrides everything below — surface first. Session mapping: regular_hours needs the matched account_type_tradability='tradable'; extended_hours / all_day_hours need all_day_tradability='tradable'; 24/7 needs twenty_four_seven_tradability='tradable' (a separate field, omitted when 24/7 does not apply). Mention internal_halt_* only when internal_halt_sessions overlaps the session the user wants. Fractional and dollar-based orders place only in regular_hours regardless of the flags. See trading://market-hours for session clock times.
  guide: string;
}>>; };
```
